4. PHOTOGRAPHS — individual licences, see src/data/photo-credits.json
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The 24 photographs in public/photos/ come from Wikimedia Commons and remain
under their own individual licences: CC0, public domain, CC BY 2.0, CC BY 4.0,
CC BY-SA 3.0 and CC BY-SA 4.0. 22 of the 24 require attribution. Twenty are
landmarks; four (Task 5a) are each state's own animal, one photograph per
distinct species so two places naming the same species share it rather than
each fetching their own.

Per-file artist, licence, licence URL, source page and ready-to-render
attribution are in src/data/photo-credits.json, and are displayed in the app
at #/credits.

NOT MODIFIED: each file is a thumbnail rendered by Wikimedia's own servers and
stored byte for byte as it was delivered. That is a change of format and size,
not of content, so none of these is an adaptation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. SOUNDS — individual licences, see src/data/sound-credits.json
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The 11 sounds in public/audio/ come from Wikimedia Commons and remain under
their own individual licences: CC0, public domain, CC BY-SA 3.0 and
CC BY-SA 4.0. 7 of the 11 require attribution.

Per-file artist, licence, licence URL, source page, ready-to-render
attribution and a description of what was changed are in
src/data/sound-credits.json, and are displayed in the app at #/credits.

MODIFIED: every one of them. One-shots are truncated to a cap, peak-normalised
to -1 dBFS and given a 150 ms fade-out (scripts/lib/trim.py); ambient beds are
truncated to 20 s, loudness-normalised to -26 dBFS RMS under a -3 dBFS peak
ceiling, and welded into a seamless loop with a 3 s equal-power crossfade
(scripts/lib/loop.py). All are then decoded to mono and re-encoded as AAC.

Cutting and levelling change the content, so these are Adapted Material.
Accordingly, the seven files below — the modified versions, not the originals
— are offered under the same licence as their sources:

    public/audio/ambience/ocean.m4a          CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/ambience/forest.m4a         CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/sfx/peacock-call.m4a        CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/sfx/hornbill.m4a            CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/sfx/indian-roller.m4a       CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/sfx/gibbon.m4a              CC BY-SA 4.0
    public/audio/sfx/sparrow.m4a             CC BY-SA 3.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. NARRATION AUDIO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The narration in public/audio/en/ is synthesised from the scripts in
content/, which are MIT with the code. It currently uses the free macOS `say`
voice; a paid ElevenLabs render is subject to that provider's own terms, which
are not a licence this repository can grant. Regenerate it yourself with
`npm run tts:draft`.
